# no-serde-json (tools/ci-checks, #162, DEP-3): a ratchet. These are exactly the first-party paths that
# still name serde_json, each tagged with the slice that removes it:
#   W3-D-<task>  wave 3 of MIN-3 deletes or rewrites the path (ABI-MIN3-WBS W3-D-*; SERDE-JSON-EXIT §4);
#   D            the #162 serde_json exit converts it to busbar_contract::json (SERDE-JSON-EXIT r2 MR 6/7/9a,
#                slices S1-S7 and D; wserde-claude/SLICES.md).
# Format: one path per line, relative to the repository root, then `# <slice>`. A line ending in `/`
# covers the directory below it. A path not listed here that names serde_json fails the check, so no new
# use can land. The list only shrinks: a line under which no file names serde_json any more fails the
# check, so the converting MR deletes its line. Never add a line: move the code to busbar_contract::json.

